{
  "info": {
    "name": "Campus-Fix API",
    "description": "Colección de Postman para la API de Campus-Fix. Cubre los casos: exitoso, datos inválidos, no autenticado, sin permisos, recurso inexistente y regla de negocio incumplida (AGENTS.md §31).\n\nAntes de ejecutar: importar el environment 'Campus-Fix Local' y arrancar el backend (pnpm --filter backend dev). Los requests de Login capturan los tokens en variables de entorno; el de Registrar incidencia captura {{incidencia_id}}.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Autenticación",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login - Administrador (exitoso)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"correo\": \"carlos.mendoza@ecotec.edu.ec\",\n  \"contrasena\": \"CampusFix2026!\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/login"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.environment.set('admin_token', json.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login - Técnico (exitoso)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"correo\": \"andres.vera@ecotec.edu.ec\",\n  \"contrasena\": \"CampusFix2026!\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/login"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
